1
00:00:02,509 --> 00:00:03,551
KATARA: Water.

2
00:00:04,969 --> 00:00:06,012
Earth.

3
00:00:06,846 --> 00:00:07,889
Fire.

4
00:00:08,973 --> 00:00:10,016
Air.

5
00:00:11,184 --> 00:00:15,146
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:15,396 --> 00:00:18,775
Then, everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:19,651 --> 00:00:22,487
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

8
00:00:22,570 --> 00:00:23,780
could stop them.

9
00:00:23,863 --> 00:00:26,699
But when the world needed him most,
he vanished.

10
00:00:27,325 --> 00:00:29,786
A hundred years passed,
and my brother and I discovered

11
00:00:29,869 --> 00:00:32,872
the new Avatar, an airbender named Aang.

12
00:00:32,956 --> 00:00:35,166
And although
his airbending skills are great,

13
00:00:35,250 --> 00:00:37,502
he has a lot to learn
before he's ready to save anyone.

14
00:00:37,627 --> 00:00:38,836
AANG: Oof!

15
00:00:38,920 --> 00:00:42,090
But I believe Aang can save the world.

16
00:00:42,465 --> 00:00:44,467
♪

17
00:00:48,054 --> 00:00:50,306
( NARRATOR READING )

18
00:00:50,515 --> 00:00:52,183
Sokka's your name, right?

19
00:00:52,267 --> 00:00:55,728
My favorite prisoner used
to mention you all the time.

20
00:00:55,812 --> 00:00:58,606
She was convinced you were
going to come rescue her.

21
00:00:58,690 --> 00:01:01,609
Of course, you never came,
and she gave up on you.

22
00:01:02,986 --> 00:01:05,863
Where is Suki?

23
00:01:06,197 --> 00:01:07,907
How are we all gonna escape?

24
00:01:07,991 --> 00:01:10,410
We're not. You kids have to leave.

25
00:01:10,493 --> 00:01:12,495
You have to escape on Appa together.

26
00:01:12,579 --> 00:01:13,621
Goodbye, Dad.

27
00:01:13,705 --> 00:01:16,958
We won't be apart
for too long this time. I promise.

28
00:01:18,167 --> 00:01:19,711
( CALM MUSIC )

29
00:01:23,423 --> 00:01:24,549
♪

30
00:01:26,050 --> 00:01:27,594
ZUKO: No one can make tea like Uncle.

31
00:01:27,677 --> 00:01:29,762
But, hopefully, I learned a thing or two.

32
00:01:29,846 --> 00:01:32,181
Would you like to hear
Uncle's favorite tea joke?

33
00:01:32,265 --> 00:01:33,433
KATARA: Sure.
AANG: I like jokes.

34
00:01:33,516 --> 00:01:34,642
TOPH: Bring it!

35
00:01:35,476 --> 00:01:37,937
Okay, well, I can't
remember how it starts,

36
00:01:38,021 --> 00:01:41,733
but the punchline is
"Leaf me alone. I'm bushed!"

37
00:01:41,858 --> 00:01:42,984
( CRICKETS CHIRPING )

38
00:01:46,654 --> 00:01:49,115
Well, it's funnier when Uncle tells it.

39
00:01:49,198 --> 00:01:50,241
Right.

40
00:01:50,325 --> 00:01:52,869
Maybe that's because he
remembers the whole thing.

41
00:01:52,952 --> 00:01:55,204
( LAUGHTER )

42
00:01:59,208 --> 00:02:01,502
It's nice to get a
chance to relax a little.

43
00:02:01,586 --> 00:02:03,129
It hardly ever happens.

44
00:02:08,801 --> 00:02:10,845
Hey, can I talk to you for a second?

45
00:02:16,517 --> 00:02:18,019
So what's up?

46
00:02:18,102 --> 00:02:21,105
SOKKA: If someone was
captured by the Fire Nation,

47
00:02:21,189 --> 00:02:22,607
where would they be taken?

48
00:02:22,690 --> 00:02:24,817
ZUKO: What do you mean? Who was captured?

49
00:02:24,901 --> 00:02:28,404
When the invasion plan failed,
some of our troops were taken.

50
00:02:28,488 --> 00:02:30,615
I just want to know where they might be.

51
00:02:30,698 --> 00:02:31,866
I can't tell you.

52
00:02:31,949 --> 00:02:33,117
What? Why not?

53
00:02:33,201 --> 00:02:36,579
Trust me. Knowing will just
make you feel worse.

54
00:02:37,580 --> 00:02:40,708
It's my dad. He was captured, too.

55
00:02:40,792 --> 00:02:42,710
I need to know what I put him through.

56
00:02:42,794 --> 00:02:45,380
- It's not good, Sokka.
- Please.

57
00:02:46,047 --> 00:02:49,550
My guess is they were taken
to the Boiling Rock.

58
00:02:49,634 --> 00:02:50,677
What's that?

59
00:02:50,760 --> 00:02:53,012
ZUKO: The highest-security
prison in the Fire Nation.

60
00:02:53,930 --> 00:02:57,016
It's on an island
in the middle of the boiling lake.

61
00:02:57,100 --> 00:03:00,019
- It's inescapable.
- So where is this place?

62
00:03:00,103 --> 00:03:02,814
Why do you need to know?
What are you planning?

63
00:03:02,897 --> 00:03:03,940
Nothing.

64
00:03:04,816 --> 00:03:06,734
Boy, you're so paranoid.

65
00:03:06,818 --> 00:03:09,153
It's in the middle of a volcano

66
00:03:09,237 --> 00:03:11,489
between here and the Fire Nation.

67
00:03:11,572 --> 00:03:14,450
You guys actually flew right
past it on the way here.

68
00:03:14,534 --> 00:03:16,744
Thanks, Zuko. ( YAWNS )

69
00:03:16,828 --> 00:03:19,288
Just knowing makes me feel better.

70
00:03:19,372 --> 00:03:21,666
Yeah, I'm sure it does.

71
00:03:24,293 --> 00:03:26,421
( SNORES )

72
00:03:26,504 --> 00:03:28,339
♪

73
00:03:34,137 --> 00:03:35,346
( SIGHS )

74
00:03:35,430 --> 00:03:36,848
( GASPS )

75
00:03:36,931 --> 00:03:38,391
( SNORES )

76
00:03:38,474 --> 00:03:40,476
( WATER RUSHING )

77
00:03:43,312 --> 00:03:44,480
Shh!

78
00:03:47,775 --> 00:03:49,402
Not up to anything, huh?

79
00:03:49,485 --> 00:03:50,862
Ahh!

80
00:03:50,945 --> 00:03:52,488
-( THUD )
-( GROANS )

81
00:03:52,572 --> 00:03:54,240
Fine, you caught me.

82
00:03:54,323 --> 00:03:56,701
I'm gonna rescue my dad. You happy now?

83
00:03:56,784 --> 00:03:58,411
I'm never happy.

84
00:03:58,494 --> 00:04:02,415
Look, I have to do this.
The invasion plan was my idea.

85
00:04:02,498 --> 00:04:05,418
It was my decision to stay
when things were going wrong.

86
00:04:05,501 --> 00:04:08,796
It's my mistake,
and it's my job to fix it.

87
00:04:08,880 --> 00:04:12,425
I have to regain my honor.
You can't stop me, Zuko.

88
00:04:13,509 --> 00:04:17,096
You need to regain your honor?
Believe me, I get it.

89
00:04:17,180 --> 00:04:18,514
I'm going with you.

90
00:04:18,598 --> 00:04:21,309
No! I have to do this alone.

91
00:04:21,392 --> 00:04:24,020
How are you going to get there? On Appa?

92
00:04:24,103 --> 00:04:27,440
Last time I checked, prisons
don't have bison daycares.

93
00:04:28,024 --> 00:04:29,484
( SIGHS )

94
00:04:30,276 --> 00:04:31,986
We'll take my war balloon.

95
00:04:34,781 --> 00:04:36,449
( SNORES )

96
00:04:39,160 --> 00:04:40,787
( BIRDS CHIRPING )

97
00:04:42,163 --> 00:04:43,456
( GROWLS )

98
00:04:47,502 --> 00:04:48,669
What does it say?

99
00:04:48,795 --> 00:04:50,713
"Need meat. Gone fishing.

100
00:04:50,797 --> 00:04:52,590
"Back in a few days. Sokka and Zuko."

101
00:04:52,673 --> 00:04:53,716
( YAWNS )

102
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:55,051
"One more thing.

103
00:04:55,134 --> 00:04:57,428
"Aang, practice your firebending
while I'm gone.

104
00:04:57,553 --> 00:05:00,056
"Do 20 sets of fire fists
and 10 hop squats

105
00:05:00,139 --> 00:05:02,141
"every time you hear a badger frog croak.

106
00:05:02,225 --> 00:05:03,267
"Zuko."

107
00:05:03,768 --> 00:05:05,853
( BADGER FROG CROAKING )

108
00:05:05,937 --> 00:05:08,439
( SIGHS ) Nobody else has homework.

109
00:05:11,734 --> 00:05:15,404
One hop squat, two hop squat,
three hop squat, four hop squat...

110
00:05:19,951 --> 00:05:21,410
( FIRE RUMBLING )

111
00:05:21,494 --> 00:05:23,579
( WHIRRING )

112
00:05:29,210 --> 00:05:30,837
Pretty clouds.

113
00:05:30,920 --> 00:05:32,880
Yeah, fluffy.

114
00:05:35,633 --> 00:05:37,385
( SOKKA WHISTLING )

115
00:05:37,468 --> 00:05:38,511
What?

116
00:05:38,594 --> 00:05:41,013
What? Oh, I didn't say anything.

117
00:05:42,390 --> 00:05:45,393
You know, a friend of mine
actually designed these war balloons.

118
00:05:45,476 --> 00:05:46,602
No kidding.

119
00:05:46,686 --> 00:05:50,147
Yup. A balloon, but for war.

120
00:05:50,231 --> 00:05:53,359
If there's one thing my
dad's good at, it's war.

121
00:05:53,442 --> 00:05:55,653
Yeah, it seems to run in the family.

122
00:05:55,736 --> 00:05:56,779
Hey, hold on.

123
00:05:56,863 --> 00:05:58,698
Not everyone in my family is like that.

124
00:05:58,781 --> 00:06:00,908
I know, I know. You've changed.

125
00:06:01,367 --> 00:06:03,536
I meant my uncle.

126
00:06:03,619 --> 00:06:05,872
He was more of a father to me.

127
00:06:05,955 --> 00:06:07,832
And I really let him down.

128
00:06:08,708 --> 00:06:10,793
I think your uncle would be proud of you.

129
00:06:10,877 --> 00:06:12,628
Leaving your home to come help us?

130
00:06:12,712 --> 00:06:13,796
That's hard.

131
00:06:14,881 --> 00:06:16,424
It wasn't that hard.

132
00:06:16,507 --> 00:06:19,594
Really? You didn't leave behind
anyone you cared about?

133
00:06:19,719 --> 00:06:23,097
Well, I did have a girlfriend, Mai.

134
00:06:23,180 --> 00:06:25,474
That gloomy girl who sighs a lot?

135
00:06:25,558 --> 00:06:26,642
Yeah.

136
00:06:28,185 --> 00:06:30,897
Everyone in the Fire Nation
thinks I'm a traitor.

137
00:06:30,980 --> 00:06:32,648
I couldn't drag her into it.

138
00:06:34,275 --> 00:06:36,360
My first girlfriend turned into the moon.

139
00:06:37,778 --> 00:06:39,030
That's rough, buddy.

140
00:06:43,492 --> 00:06:45,494
( SNORES )

141
00:06:47,038 --> 00:06:49,165
( FIRE RUMBLING )

142
00:06:49,248 --> 00:06:52,376
( WHIRRING )

143
00:06:52,460 --> 00:06:54,211
- There it is.
- Huh? Huh?

144
00:06:54,837 --> 00:06:57,006
There's plenty of
steam to keep us covered.

145
00:06:57,089 --> 00:06:59,216
As long as we're quiet,
we should be able to navigate

146
00:06:59,300 --> 00:07:00,885
through it without being caught.

147
00:07:00,968 --> 00:07:02,970
( ADVENTUROUS MUSIC )

148
00:07:03,930 --> 00:07:05,765
♪

149
00:07:20,154 --> 00:07:21,405
We're going down.

150
00:07:21,489 --> 00:07:22,907
The balloon's not working anymore.

151
00:07:24,158 --> 00:07:26,535
SOKKA: The air outside
is just as hot as the air inside,

152
00:07:26,619 --> 00:07:28,120
so we can't fly.

153
00:07:28,663 --> 00:07:29,705
Whoa!

154
00:07:29,789 --> 00:07:31,499
So what are we supposed to do?

155
00:07:31,582 --> 00:07:33,960
I don't know. Crash landing?

156
00:07:36,504 --> 00:07:37,713
( SPLASHING )

157
00:07:38,172 --> 00:07:39,715
( YELPS )

158
00:07:43,469 --> 00:07:44,637
( GROANING )

159
00:07:47,932 --> 00:07:49,266
( SPUTTERS )

160
00:07:50,601 --> 00:07:52,311
ZUKO: How are we gonna get off the island

161
00:07:52,395 --> 00:07:53,646
if the balloon won't work?

162
00:07:53,729 --> 00:07:55,231
SOKKA: We'll figure something out.

163
00:07:55,314 --> 00:07:57,400
I suspected it might be a one-way ticket.

164
00:07:57,483 --> 00:08:00,361
You knew this would happen
and you wanted to come anyway?

165
00:08:00,444 --> 00:08:03,614
My dad might be here.
I had to come and see.

166
00:08:03,698 --> 00:08:05,992
ZUKO: Uncle always said I never
thought things through.

167
00:08:06,075 --> 00:08:07,827
But this? ( SIGHS )

168
00:08:07,910 --> 00:08:09,620
This is just crazy!

169
00:08:09,704 --> 00:08:12,790
Hey, I never wanted you
to come along in the first place.

170
00:08:12,873 --> 00:08:15,668
And for the record,
I always think things through.

171
00:08:15,751 --> 00:08:17,545
But my plans haven't exactly worked.

172
00:08:17,628 --> 00:08:19,630
So this time, I'm playing it by ear.

173
00:08:19,714 --> 00:08:20,881
So there!

174
00:08:20,965 --> 00:08:22,425
-( SIZZLING )
- Aah!

175
00:08:25,094 --> 00:08:27,013
ZUKO: What are you doing?

176
00:08:27,096 --> 00:08:30,558
It doesn't work anyway, and
we don't want anyone to find it.

177
00:08:30,641 --> 00:08:33,310
I hope you know what you're doing.

178
00:08:33,394 --> 00:08:35,021
There's no turning back now.

179
00:08:45,823 --> 00:08:47,533
( CREAKING )

180
00:08:47,742 --> 00:08:49,618
I hope these disguises work.

181
00:08:49,702 --> 00:08:52,788
We just need to lay low and
find my dad as soon as possible.

182
00:08:55,207 --> 00:08:57,043
Guards! There's a scuffle in the yard.

183
00:08:57,126 --> 00:08:58,377
Come on!

184
00:08:59,045 --> 00:09:01,964
♪

185
00:09:06,427 --> 00:09:09,680
I didn't do anything.
I'm going back to my cell.

186
00:09:11,432 --> 00:09:13,350
Stop right there, Chit Sang!

187
00:09:15,686 --> 00:09:17,396
We can't blow our cover.

188
00:09:19,440 --> 00:09:21,942
I've had it with your unruly behavior.

189
00:09:22,026 --> 00:09:23,527
What did I do?

190
00:09:23,611 --> 00:09:26,864
He wants to know what he did.
Isn't that cute?

191
00:09:30,117 --> 00:09:33,120
- Uh, yeah, very cute, sir.
- Super cute.

192
00:09:33,871 --> 00:09:37,124
You didn't bow down
when I walked by, Chit Sang.

193
00:09:37,208 --> 00:09:39,585
What? That's not a prison rule.

194
00:09:39,668 --> 00:09:40,836
Do it!

195
00:09:41,879 --> 00:09:42,963
Make me.

196
00:09:47,426 --> 00:09:49,386
( INDISTINCT CHATTER )

197
00:09:50,971 --> 00:09:53,140
( FIRE RUMBLING )

198
00:09:57,770 --> 00:09:59,146
( CLUCKS TONGUE )

199
00:09:59,230 --> 00:10:03,275
Firebending is prohibited.
You're goin' in the cooler.

200
00:10:04,985 --> 00:10:07,154
You! Help me take him in.

201
00:10:07,780 --> 00:10:09,448
Meet back here in an hour.

202
00:10:09,824 --> 00:10:13,244
♪

203
00:10:20,835 --> 00:10:22,962
The warden will deal with you soon.

204
00:10:23,045 --> 00:10:24,171
( GROANS )

205
00:10:27,633 --> 00:10:29,593
Can you believe this guy?

206
00:10:29,677 --> 00:10:31,887
Prisoners! Am I right?

207
00:10:31,971 --> 00:10:33,889
( GROWLS ) Tell me about it.

208
00:10:33,973 --> 00:10:36,142
( INDISTINCT CHATTER )

209
00:10:37,017 --> 00:10:39,145
Ha-ha! Hey, new guy!

210
00:10:39,228 --> 00:10:41,564
I know it's the rule to have
your helmet on at all times,

211
00:10:41,647 --> 00:10:43,149
but this is the lounge.

212
00:10:43,232 --> 00:10:44,483
Relax!

213
00:10:44,567 --> 00:10:46,485
But what if there's an incident?

214
00:10:46,569 --> 00:10:48,988
If I'm not prepared, someone
could strike me on the head.

215
00:10:49,071 --> 00:10:54,076
( LAUGHTER )

216
00:10:54,160 --> 00:10:56,495
Give it a week. He'll loosen up.

217
00:10:57,163 --> 00:10:58,789
Can the new guy ask you veterans

218
00:10:58,873 --> 00:11:00,457
a few questions about the prison?

219
00:11:00,541 --> 00:11:03,669
No, you can't date the female guards.

220
00:11:03,794 --> 00:11:06,297
Trust me, you don't want to.

221
00:11:06,380 --> 00:11:07,756
-( SMACK )
-( LAUGHS )

222
00:11:07,840 --> 00:11:09,633
No, that's not it.

223
00:11:09,717 --> 00:11:11,427
The Boiling Rock.

224
00:11:11,510 --> 00:11:14,263
It holds the Fire Nation's
most dangerous criminals, right?

225
00:11:15,389 --> 00:11:17,266
So what about war prisoners?

226
00:11:19,935 --> 00:11:21,437
( OMINOUS MUSIC )

227
00:11:21,520 --> 00:11:24,565
♪

228
00:11:27,568 --> 00:11:29,570
( WHOOSH )

229
00:11:33,532 --> 00:11:35,201
( PANTS )

230
00:11:38,412 --> 00:11:40,372
It sure looks cold in there.

231
00:11:40,456 --> 00:11:42,708
That's why we call it the cooler.

232
00:11:42,791 --> 00:11:44,668
He won't be firebending in there.

233
00:11:44,752 --> 00:11:45,794
( FOOTSTEPS )

234
00:11:45,878 --> 00:11:47,713
It's the warden! Look alive!

235
00:11:47,796 --> 00:11:49,798
♪

236
00:11:52,593 --> 00:11:57,097
So, Chit Sang, I hear you used
firebending to try to escape.

237
00:11:57,181 --> 00:11:58,557
You should know better.

238
00:11:58,641 --> 00:12:00,976
I wasn't trying to escape.

239
00:12:01,060 --> 00:12:03,812
MALE GUARD: He's lying!
I saw him with my own eyes.

240
00:12:04,688 --> 00:12:07,691
No one has ever, ever escaped from here.

241
00:12:07,775 --> 00:12:10,027
I'd sooner jump in the boiling lake myself

242
00:12:10,110 --> 00:12:12,029
than let that record fall.

243
00:12:12,112 --> 00:12:13,989
Don't forget it.

244
00:12:14,073 --> 00:12:15,991
Now go back to your shivering.

245
00:12:16,617 --> 00:12:18,744
-( DOOR SHUTS )
-( SHIVERING )

246
00:12:20,746 --> 00:12:22,748
( INDISTINCT CHATTER )

247
00:12:24,625 --> 00:12:28,545
Hey, there, fellow guard. How goes it?

248
00:12:28,629 --> 00:12:29,672
Zuko?

249
00:12:29,755 --> 00:12:30,798
Shh!

250
00:12:30,923 --> 00:12:33,092
Listen, I asked around the lounge.

251
00:12:33,175 --> 00:12:35,469
There are no Water Tribe prisoners.

252
00:12:35,552 --> 00:12:37,304
I'm afraid your father's not here.

253
00:12:37,388 --> 00:12:38,847
What? Are you sure?

254
00:12:38,931 --> 00:12:40,266
Did you double check?

255
00:12:40,349 --> 00:12:42,226
Yeah, I'm sure.

256
00:12:42,309 --> 00:12:44,937
No. No!

257
00:12:45,312 --> 00:12:46,897
I'm really sorry, Sokka.

258
00:12:47,022 --> 00:12:49,566
So we came all this way for nothing?

259
00:12:49,650 --> 00:12:51,735
I failed... again.

260
00:12:52,444 --> 00:12:54,238
Ah, what would Uncle say?

261
00:12:56,448 --> 00:12:59,952
Sometimes clouds have two sides,
a dark and light,

262
00:13:00,035 --> 00:13:02,162
and a silver lining in between.

263
00:13:02,246 --> 00:13:03,998
It's like a silver sandwich.

264
00:13:04,081 --> 00:13:09,461
So when life seems hard,
take a bite out of the silver sandwich.

265
00:13:11,839 --> 00:13:13,799
Maybe we haven't failed after all!

266
00:13:13,882 --> 00:13:16,635
That's the spirit!
I can't believe that worked.

267
00:13:16,719 --> 00:13:18,554
I didn't even know what I was saying.

268
00:13:18,637 --> 00:13:20,264
No, what you said made no sense at all.

269
00:13:20,347 --> 00:13:21,390
But look!

270
00:13:22,057 --> 00:13:23,434
It's Suki!

271
00:13:23,517 --> 00:13:25,185
MALE GUARD: Prisoners! Back in your cells!

272
00:13:25,269 --> 00:13:27,313
( BELL RINGING )

273
00:13:29,106 --> 00:13:30,357
( WHIRRING )

274
00:13:32,318 --> 00:13:34,320
( MOPPING SOUNDS )

275
00:13:39,867 --> 00:13:42,578
( DOOR OPENS AND SHUTS )

276
00:13:42,661 --> 00:13:45,289
What is it? Did I do something wrong?

277
00:13:45,372 --> 00:13:46,957
You mean you don't recognize me?

278
00:13:47,041 --> 00:13:49,168
You people all look the same to me.

279
00:13:49,251 --> 00:13:51,545
Oh? Then maybe you'll recognize this.

280
00:13:51,628 --> 00:13:53,797
-( HARPS )
-( SMOOCHING SOUNDS )

281
00:13:54,882 --> 00:13:56,550
( GROANS )

282
00:13:56,925 --> 00:13:59,428
Sokka! It's you!

283
00:14:03,515 --> 00:14:05,934
The other Kyoshi Warriors, are they here?

284
00:14:06,018 --> 00:14:07,978
No. I don't know where they are.

285
00:14:08,062 --> 00:14:10,064
They locked me in here,
because I'm the leader.

286
00:14:10,147 --> 00:14:13,275
Well, you won't be here for long.
I'm busting you out.

287
00:14:13,359 --> 00:14:17,029
I'm so glad to see you, Sokka.
I knew you'd come.

288
00:14:20,324 --> 00:14:21,533
( FOOTSTEPS )

289
00:14:21,617 --> 00:14:22,910
( CLANGING )

290
00:14:26,747 --> 00:14:29,166
Excuse me. I need to get into that cell.

291
00:14:29,249 --> 00:14:30,626
No, you can't go in there.

292
00:14:31,877 --> 00:14:33,337
The lights are out.

293
00:14:33,420 --> 00:14:34,713
The prisoner could sneak up on you.

294
00:14:36,507 --> 00:14:38,300
Step aside, fool!

295
00:14:38,384 --> 00:14:40,094
Hey, hey, what are you doing?

296
00:14:41,261 --> 00:14:42,471
( ZUKO GROANS )

297
00:14:42,554 --> 00:14:43,931
( CLANGING )

298
00:14:44,807 --> 00:14:48,227
( GROANING )

299
00:14:49,728 --> 00:14:51,897
Guard, help! I think he's an imposter!

300
00:14:51,980 --> 00:14:53,732
Aah! Arrest him!

301
00:15:02,908 --> 00:15:04,910
Get him off me and arrest him!

302
00:15:04,993 --> 00:15:06,995
( GROANING )

303
00:15:10,833 --> 00:15:12,209
You're under arrest!

304
00:15:13,627 --> 00:15:15,462
Don't worry. I'll figure it out.

305
00:15:18,924 --> 00:15:20,926
( BOILING )

306
00:15:22,970 --> 00:15:24,638
( DOOR OPENS )

307
00:15:24,721 --> 00:15:26,849
Well, well, well.

308
00:15:27,391 --> 00:15:31,311
I never thought I'd find you
in here, Prince Zuko.

309
00:15:31,979 --> 00:15:33,605
How did you know who I am?

310
00:15:33,689 --> 00:15:37,985
How could I not?
You broke my niece's heart.

311
00:15:38,819 --> 00:15:40,237
You're Mai's uncle?

312
00:15:40,696 --> 00:15:42,030
I never meant to hurt her.

313
00:15:42,114 --> 00:15:43,490
Quiet!

314
00:15:43,574 --> 00:15:48,579
You're my special prisoner now.
And you best behave.

315
00:15:48,662 --> 00:15:51,498
If these criminals found out who you are,

316
00:15:51,582 --> 00:15:55,294
the traitor prince
who let his nation down,

317
00:15:55,377 --> 00:15:57,754
why, they'd tear you to shreds.

318
00:15:57,838 --> 00:15:59,381
So what's in it for you?

319
00:15:59,465 --> 00:16:02,050
Why don't you just tell my father
and collect a reward?

320
00:16:02,134 --> 00:16:06,346
Oh, in due time, believe me.
I intend to collect.

321
00:16:11,977 --> 00:16:13,896
( FOOTSTEPS )

322
00:16:17,691 --> 00:16:19,526
Oh, good. You guys have met.

323
00:16:19,610 --> 00:16:21,612
Actually, we met a long time ago.

324
00:16:21,695 --> 00:16:23,238
We did?

325
00:16:23,322 --> 00:16:26,533
Yeah, you kinda burned down my village.

326
00:16:27,910 --> 00:16:31,288
Oh, sorry about that.
Nice to see you again.

327
00:16:35,501 --> 00:16:37,878
So listen, I think I have an escape plan.

328
00:16:38,670 --> 00:16:40,339
I checked out the coolers again.

329
00:16:40,422 --> 00:16:43,383
The whole point of them
is to keep firebenders contained, right?

330
00:16:43,467 --> 00:16:44,551
Yeah.

331
00:16:44,635 --> 00:16:47,012
So they're completely insulated and sealed

332
00:16:47,095 --> 00:16:48,597
to keep the cold in.

333
00:16:48,680 --> 00:16:50,224
Well, to keep the cold in,

334
00:16:50,307 --> 00:16:52,684
it also has to keep the heat out, right?

335
00:16:52,768 --> 00:16:54,520
Just get to the point, Sokka.

336
00:16:54,603 --> 00:16:55,938
It's a perfect boat

337
00:16:56,021 --> 00:16:57,689
for getting through the boiling water.

338
00:16:59,358 --> 00:17:01,818
The cooler as a boat? Are you sure?

339
00:17:01,902 --> 00:17:03,737
I'm telling you, it'll work.

340
00:17:05,989 --> 00:17:07,699
I walked around the perimeter.

341
00:17:07,783 --> 00:17:10,577
There's a blind spot
between two guard towers.

342
00:17:10,661 --> 00:17:12,704
It's the perfect launching point.

343
00:17:13,747 --> 00:17:15,666
I already tested it out.

344
00:17:15,791 --> 00:17:17,834
We'll roll the cooler into the water

345
00:17:17,960 --> 00:17:21,255
and just float with the current.
It'll take us straight across.

346
00:17:21,380 --> 00:17:23,840
As long as we don't make a sound,
no one will notice.

347
00:17:23,966 --> 00:17:26,134
And bing, bang, boom, we're home free!

348
00:17:26,218 --> 00:17:28,512
But how are you gonna get the cooler out?

349
00:17:28,595 --> 00:17:31,306
Yeah, how are you
gonna get the cooler out?

350
00:17:33,725 --> 00:17:36,645
What? We didn't... We didn't say that!

351
00:17:36,728 --> 00:17:38,272
Yeah, you heard wrong.

352
00:17:38,355 --> 00:17:41,567
I heard you hatching
an escape plan, and I want in.

353
00:17:41,650 --> 00:17:43,485
There's nothing to get in on.

354
00:17:43,569 --> 00:17:47,531
Yeah, the only thing
we're hatching is... an egg?

355
00:17:48,031 --> 00:17:49,449
( SIGHING )

356
00:17:49,533 --> 00:17:51,410
Okay, well, I come with you,

357
00:17:51,535 --> 00:17:53,787
or the warden hears about this egg, too.

358
00:17:53,912 --> 00:17:55,872
I guess we have no choice.

359
00:17:55,956 --> 00:17:57,541
Okay, you're in.

360
00:17:57,624 --> 00:18:00,627
Now, first we need someone
to unbolt the cooler

361
00:18:00,752 --> 00:18:02,212
from the inside.

362
00:18:03,213 --> 00:18:05,215
Oh, I can get you inside.

363
00:18:06,592 --> 00:18:08,594
( INDISTINCT CHATTER )

364
00:18:11,847 --> 00:18:13,015
( GROANS )

365
00:18:13,098 --> 00:18:14,975
Hey, what are you? Stupid?

366
00:18:15,058 --> 00:18:16,560
Watch where you're going!

367
00:18:16,643 --> 00:18:18,228
( GROANING )

368
00:18:18,312 --> 00:18:20,480
Hey, you watch who you're shoving!

369
00:18:23,025 --> 00:18:25,694
I think you mean whom I'm shoving.

370
00:18:25,902 --> 00:18:29,114
( GRUNTING )

371
00:18:29,197 --> 00:18:31,199
( CHEERING )

372
00:18:34,411 --> 00:18:36,330
( GROANING )

373
00:18:36,622 --> 00:18:38,540
I need backup over here!

374
00:18:38,624 --> 00:18:40,292
( GRUNTS )

375
00:18:41,126 --> 00:18:42,753
( FIRE RUMBLING )

376
00:18:43,587 --> 00:18:46,214
No firebending. Into the cooler!

377
00:18:47,215 --> 00:18:48,508
( GROANS )

378
00:18:49,509 --> 00:18:51,553
( TENSE MUSIC )

379
00:18:52,179 --> 00:18:54,181
♪

380
00:19:04,191 --> 00:19:06,401
( GUSTING )

381
00:19:07,235 --> 00:19:08,779
I can take you back to your cell

382
00:19:08,862 --> 00:19:10,280
if you've learned your lesson.

383
00:19:11,365 --> 00:19:12,991
( FIRE RUMBLING )

384
00:19:13,075 --> 00:19:16,370
Yes, I have. Completely.

385
00:19:17,788 --> 00:19:19,331
I got Suki and Chit Sang

386
00:19:19,414 --> 00:19:21,041
out of their cells a few minutes ago.

387
00:19:21,124 --> 00:19:23,752
They'll be waiting for us at the shore.

388
00:19:23,835 --> 00:19:25,712
-( FOOTSTEPS )
- Someone's coming!

389
00:19:25,796 --> 00:19:28,590
Yeah, new arrivals coming in at dawn.

390
00:19:28,674 --> 00:19:32,219
- Anybody interesting?
- Nah, just the usual.

391
00:19:32,302 --> 00:19:35,180
Some robbers, couple of traitors,
some war prisoners.

392
00:19:35,263 --> 00:19:37,474
Though I did hear there might be a pirate.

393
00:19:37,557 --> 00:19:38,642
FEMALE GUARD: No foolin'!

394
00:19:38,725 --> 00:19:41,978
War prisoners. It could be your father.

395
00:19:42,646 --> 00:19:43,855
I know.

396
00:19:43,939 --> 00:19:46,149
Well, what should we do?

397
00:19:46,233 --> 00:19:48,819
Are we going ahead with the plan
or are we waiting another night?

398
00:19:48,902 --> 00:19:50,237
I don't know.

399
00:19:50,320 --> 00:19:52,739
Is it right for me to risk Suki's freedom,

400
00:19:52,823 --> 00:19:54,116
all of our freedom,

401
00:19:54,199 --> 00:19:56,451
on the slim chance
that my dad is gonna show up?

402
00:19:56,535 --> 00:19:57,828
It's your call, Sokka.

403
00:19:59,788 --> 00:20:01,081
( BOILING )

404
00:20:01,164 --> 00:20:03,500
♪

405
00:20:08,422 --> 00:20:10,424
Took you guys long enough.

406
00:20:10,507 --> 00:20:12,175
This here's my girl and my best buddy.

407
00:20:12,259 --> 00:20:13,385
They're coming, too.

408
00:20:13,468 --> 00:20:15,762
Fine. Everybody in the cooler.

409
00:20:15,846 --> 00:20:16,888
Let's go.

410
00:20:17,013 --> 00:20:19,015
♪

411
00:20:25,439 --> 00:20:26,773
Are you sure you wanna go?

412
00:20:26,898 --> 00:20:29,151
You're the one who said
you wanted to redeem yourself,

413
00:20:29,234 --> 00:20:30,861
redeem your honor.

414
00:20:30,944 --> 00:20:32,988
Rescuing your dad is your chance.

415
00:20:33,071 --> 00:20:34,364
Your dad?

416
00:20:35,323 --> 00:20:37,993
If I had just cut my losses
at the invasion,

417
00:20:38,076 --> 00:20:40,370
maybe we wouldn't be in this mess.

418
00:20:40,454 --> 00:20:41,913
Maybe sometimes it's just better

419
00:20:41,997 --> 00:20:43,749
to call it quits before you fail.

420
00:20:43,832 --> 00:20:45,041
No, it's not.

421
00:20:45,167 --> 00:20:47,043
Look, Sokka, you're going to fail a lot

422
00:20:47,127 --> 00:20:48,587
before things work out.

423
00:20:48,670 --> 00:20:50,714
That's supposed to make me feel better?

424
00:20:50,797 --> 00:20:52,340
Even though you'll probably fail

425
00:20:52,424 --> 00:20:54,342
over and over and over again...

426
00:20:54,426 --> 00:20:58,138
- Seriously, not helping.
-...you have to try every time.

427
00:20:58,221 --> 00:21:01,183
You can't quit because
you're afraid you might fail.

428
00:21:01,266 --> 00:21:04,644
Hey, if you two are done cuddling,
can we get a move on?

429
00:21:05,896 --> 00:21:07,939
No, I'm staying.

430
00:21:08,023 --> 00:21:12,110
You guys go. You've been here long enough.

431
00:21:12,194 --> 00:21:14,237
I'm not leaving without you, Sokka.

432
00:21:14,321 --> 00:21:15,655
I'm staying, too.

433
00:21:15,739 --> 00:21:17,491
Not me. I'm out.

434
00:21:17,574 --> 00:21:18,825
Let's roll, baby.

435
00:21:18,909 --> 00:21:20,285
( SPLASH )

436
00:21:20,869 --> 00:21:23,121
ZUKO: We gave up
our only chance of escaping.

437
00:21:23,997 --> 00:21:26,750
I hope we haven't
just made a huge mistake.

438
00:21:31,379 --> 00:21:32,798
( BOILING )

439
00:21:37,677 --> 00:21:40,180
Ah, this current is so slow.

440
00:21:41,681 --> 00:21:43,683
I can use this to paddle.

441
00:21:43,767 --> 00:21:44,976
( GRUNTS )

442
00:21:46,102 --> 00:21:48,772
( SIZZLING )

443
00:21:49,439 --> 00:21:51,942
( SCREAMS )

444
00:21:53,985 --> 00:21:55,862
( BELL CLANGING )

445
00:21:56,988 --> 00:22:00,575
Guards, secure the perimeter
and lock down the prisoners!

446
00:22:00,659 --> 00:22:01,743
Now!

447
00:22:02,702 --> 00:22:04,579
( FIRE RUMBLING )

448
00:22:07,833 --> 00:22:10,252
The plan failed! They're caught!

449
00:22:11,044 --> 00:22:13,839
Get the fugitives
and throw them in the cooler!

450
00:22:13,922 --> 00:22:16,299
Uh, they are in a cooler, sir.

451
00:22:16,383 --> 00:22:19,302
One that's bolted down
and not floating in the water!

452
00:22:19,386 --> 00:22:22,681
This is a lockdown!
We have new prisoners arriving.

453
00:22:22,764 --> 00:22:25,433
Everything must be completely secure.

454
00:22:25,517 --> 00:22:26,852
( CLANKING )

455
00:22:28,478 --> 00:22:30,146
( SPLASH )

456
00:22:30,230 --> 00:22:31,439
( TENSE MUSIC )

457
00:22:31,523 --> 00:22:33,233
♪

458
00:22:38,446 --> 00:22:40,031
The gondola's moving.

459
00:22:40,115 --> 00:22:43,660
( WHIRRING )

460
00:22:43,743 --> 00:22:46,121
♪

461
00:22:50,584 --> 00:22:51,835
This is it.

462
00:22:55,130 --> 00:22:56,673
( CLANK )

463
00:22:56,756 --> 00:22:59,593
If my dad's not there,
we risked everything for nothing.

464
00:22:59,676 --> 00:23:01,011
We had to.

465
00:23:02,095 --> 00:23:03,889
Come on, come on!

466
00:23:04,431 --> 00:23:05,765
( CLANK )

467
00:23:07,183 --> 00:23:08,351
ZUKO: Is that him?

468
00:23:08,435 --> 00:23:11,021
My dad doesn't have a nose ring.

469
00:23:14,065 --> 00:23:15,317
Where is he?

470
00:23:18,570 --> 00:23:20,864
That's it? That can't be it.

471
00:23:20,947 --> 00:23:22,449
I'm sorry, Sokka.

472
00:23:22,532 --> 00:23:24,159
Oh, no!

473
00:23:24,409 --> 00:23:27,579
MALE GUARD: Hey, you! Get off the gondola!

474
00:23:27,662 --> 00:23:31,166
♪

475
00:23:39,341 --> 00:23:40,467
Dad.

476
00:23:51,199 --> 00:23:54,202
( MALE VOCALIZING DRUMBEATS )

477
00:24:02,836 --> 00:24:04,838
♪

478
00:24:17,600 --> 00:24:19,602
♪
